Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 18:54:35 +0900
Subject: [clangd] Module preamble policy follows the attached prerequisites

The module preamble policy is resolved on the update worker and follows the prerequisites actually attached to the preamble; asynchronous trace spans own the preamble filenames they retain.

* [clangd] Resolve module preamble policy on the update worker

* [clangd] Own preamble filenames retained by asynchronous trace spans

  JSON StringRef metadata borrows the caller storage, while a callback can retain the tracing context beyond buildPreamble return. Own the filename at both preamble trace attachment sites and exercise an actual retained callback context with caller storage overwritten before event serialization.

* fix(clangd): preamble mode follows attached module prerequisites
